## 4. INTENDED USE AND PERMITTED ACTIVITIES

**4.1 Intended Use.** MyTake5 is intended solely as a
supplementary pre-task hazard identification and documentation
tool to support — not replace — the professional judgement of a
competent person at a worksite.

**4.2 Permitted Activities.** Subscribers and Users may use the
Service to:

(a) Complete digital Take 5 pre-task risk assessments;

(b) Identify and document workplace hazards and controls;

(c) Generate PDF and JSON records of completed Take 5 assessments;

(d) Use the AI-assisted work area scan as an observational aid
    for hazard identification.

**4.3 Prohibited Activities.** Subscribers and Users must NOT:

(a) Use the Service as the sole or primary risk assessment method
    for any task;

(b) Use the Service in place of, or as a substitute for, Safe Work
    Method Statements (SWMS), permits to work, Job Safety Analyses
    (JSA), principal mining hazard management plans, or any other
    document required by statute or site procedure;

(c) Rely upon the AI-assisted scan as a risk assessment or as
    evidence of any hazard in any legal, regulatory, insurance or
    disciplinary proceeding;

(d) Modify, tamper with, reverse engineer or decompile the Service;

(e) Share, transfer, sell or sublicence the company code to any
    person or organisation outside the Subscriber;

(f) Use the Service for any purpose that would constitute misuse
    within the meaning of s.26A of the WHS Act;

(g) Represent to any person that completion of a Take 5 using
    MyTake5 satisfies any statutory obligation independently of
    the Subscriber's own WHS management system.

